I made a few changes to your commit during review:

- The `dialog` controller now waits only for the exit transitions of the `<dialog>` and its `::backdrop`. `getAnimations({ subtree: true })` also returned the endless animations of the content (a spinner, a skeleton), so the dialog never closed.
- A timeout now closes the dialog if a transition never finishes. Each close gets its own token, so a promise or timer left over from an earlier close cannot end a later exit early.
- `open()` now calls `showModal()` when the `<dialog>` was closed natively during the exit. Before, it only removed `data-closing` and the dialog stayed closed.
- The `dialog`, `sheet` and `drawer` templates no longer transition `display` and `overlay`. Now that the controller plays the exit, these transitions kept the closed `<dialog>` in the top layer for one more full duration in Chromium and Safari.

Six new specs cover these cases, and the dialog, sheet and drawer specs pass in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.
